- op: discuss  # cf91
  at: '2026-08-18T23:22:43Z'  # cf91
  by: agent  # cf91
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cf91
  clock: 3  # cf91
  nonce: cf91  # cf91
  message: "Closed by PR #413 (merged, dev@d555891ab2). Repro re-run on the MERGED tree, both arms:\n\n  $ hypergumbo survey . --backend rust-analyzer --out /tmp/ra3.json\n    \"installed but NOT enabled\" occurrences: 0   (was 1)\n    \"rust-analyzer backend ACTIVE for this run\": 1\n    scip-origin edges in the artifact: 2         (backend genuinely ran, as before)\n\n  $ hypergumbo survey . --out /tmp/ts3.json      # default path, control\n    \"installed but NOT enabled\" occurrences: 1   (unchanged -- the nudge is WANTED here)\n\nRoot cause: check_rust_analyzer_disclosure branched on `available` (binary on\nPATH) alone and never consulted the opt-in gate. It now takes an `enabled`\nargument, resolved at the call site from HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER exactly the\nway `available` is resolved -- cli.py normalises --backend rust-analyzer into\nthat env var during argv pre-parse, so one signal covers both opt-in routes.\n\nFix shape chosen deliberately: the warning is KEPT rather than suppressed. Its\npayload is a security disclosure (indexing executes the workspace's build.rs\nand proc macros as the invoking user; the docstring records that sandboxing\nwas tried, measured, and reverted). Suppressing on the enabled path would have\ndiscarded it. The caveat now appears in every arm that speaks, and in the\nenabled arm it is phrased in the present tense because there it describes what\nis happening rather than what would happen on opt-in.\n\nDisclosed duplication: the truthy value set for the env var is authoritative in\ngate._TRUTHY_VALUES, inside the OPTIONAL rust-analyzer package, which core\ncannot import -- core must decide what to print whether or not that package is\ninstalled. Core carries a copy, pinned to the original by\ntest_enabled_truthiness_matches_the_gates_own_vocabulary so a drift fails in\nCI rather than silently in a user's terminal.\n\nCoverage: 4 new tests (enabled-suppresses, disabled-still-fires as the positive\ncontrol, caveat-survives-every-arm, no-Rust-says-nothing) plus the parity test.\n4074 passed."  # cf91
